# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
myFromPairsFunction(pairs);
utils.object.foo(pairs);
_.fromPairs(pairs);

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.js:2:1 lint/nursery/useObjectFromEntries  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This call to myFromPairsFunction() builds an object from a list of key-value pairs.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ myFromPairsFunction(pairs);
      │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ utils.object.foo(pairs);
    4 │ _.fromPairs(pairs);
  
  i Object.fromEntries() does the same thing and is built into JavaScript, so no helper function is needed.
  
  i Call Object.fromEntries() instead.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use Object.fromEntries() instead.
  
    1 1 │   /* should generate diagnostics */
    2   │ - myFromPairsFunction(pairs);
      2 │ + Object.fromEntries(pairs);
    3 3 │   utils.object.foo(pairs);
    4 4 │   _.fromPairs(pairs);
  

```

